{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_015EePBQyVKC2qpPPNcahsvG", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wi-Fi\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.portnox.com/?p=17663\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.portnox.com/?p=14263\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.portnox.com/blog/security-trends/origin-of-wifi/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.tomsguide.com/features/think-you-know-what-wi-fi-stands-for-get-ready-for-a-surprise\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.travelweek.ca/news/do-you-even-know-what-wi-fi-stands-for/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://gizmodo.com.au/?p=1942608\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.travelweek.ca/?p=68870\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:04:12.460Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Wi-Fi name coined by Interbrand brand consulting firm", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01EQdwRgp2X7rzdk47YMK5yd", "content": [{"title": "Wi-Fi", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wi-Fi"}, {"title": "The Origin of the Word “Wi-Fi”: A Dive into Tech Etymology", "url": "https://www.portnox.com/?p=17663"}, {"title": "The Origin of the Word “Wi-Fi”: A Dive into Tech Etymology", "url": "https://www.portnox.com/?p=14263"}, {"title": "The Origin of the Word “Wi-Fi”: A Dive into Tech Etymology", "url": "https://www.portnox.com/blog/security-trends/origin-of-wifi/"}, {"title": "Think you know what Wi-Fi stands for? Get ready for a surprise", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/features/think-you-know-what-wi-fi-stands-for-get-ready-for-a-surprise"}, {"title": "Do you even know what Wi-Fi stands for?", "url": "https://www.travelweek.ca/news/do-you-even-know-what-wi-fi-stands-for/"}, {"title": "gizmodo.com.au", "url": "https://gizmodo.com.au/?p=1942608"}, {"title": "Do you even know what Wi-Fi stands for?", "url": "https://www.travelweek.ca/?p=68870"}, {"title": "boingboing.net", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html/amp"}, {"title": "boingboing.net", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp"}]}, "Interbrand, the brand consultancy, is credited with coining the name \"Wi-Fi.\"\n\n- **Origin:** Wikipedia says the name was coined by Interbrand, and that it was in commercial use by August 1999. The Wi-Fi Alliance had hired Interbrand to create a name that was \"a little catchier than 'IEEE 802.11b Direct Sequence'.\"\n- **Selection:** According to Phil Belanger, a founding member of the Wi-Fi Alliance, the alliance picked the name from a list of ten options Interbrand proposed (per Wikipedia and a 2005 Boing Boing post by Belanger).\n- **Meaning:** The name is a play on \"Hi-Fi,\" not an abbreviation. One source notes that \"Wi-Fi\" does not stand for \"Wireless Fidelity\"; it's simply a catchy, invented term designed to be reminiscent of \"Hi-Fi.\"\n- **Tagline:** The Wi-Fi Alliance added the tagline \"The Standard for Wireless Fidelity\" early on. Belanger later called this a mistake, and it was dropped about a year later (per Travel Week).\n- **Other work:** Interbrand also designed the Wi-Fi logo and, per Boing Boing, earlier brands such as Prozac and Compaq."], "durationSeconds": 4.997540290999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_015EePBQyVKC2qpPPNcahsvG", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDY3zHRhWqXXAXxTgdtm", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**答案：Interbrand（英图博略）。** 搜了 1 次。\n\n当时 Wi-Fi 联盟的前身 WECA 请 Interbrand 想一个比“IEEE 802.11b Direct Sequence”好记的名字。联盟从 Interbrand 提出的 10 个名字里选了“Wi-Fi”，1999 年 8 月前开始商用。这个名字是仿“Hi-Fi”造的词，并不是“Wireless Fidelity”的缩写。Wi-Fi 的标志也是 Interbrand 设计的。\n\n依据：\n- [Wikipedia – Wi-Fi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wi-Fi)\n- [Boing Boing（2005，Wi-Fi 联盟创始成员 Phil Belanger 的说法）](https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp)\n- [Portnox – The Origin of the Word \"Wi-Fi\"](https://www.portnox.com/blog/security-trends/origin-of-wifi/)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1198, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4292, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1198}, "output_tokens": 372, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:04:17.326Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDY3z1JeJBVG7wxP11oq"}
